#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 1: Set properties of the problem to solve {#step-1-set-properties-of-"
"the-problem-to-solve}"
msgstr ""
"Hakbang 1: Itakda ang mga properties ng problemang sosolusyunan "
"{#step-1-set-properties-of-the-problem-to-solve}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This tutorial covers the user experience from two perspectives: the\n"
"physical problem determined by the initial conditions, and the algorithmic\n"
"component in solving a fluid dynamics example on a quantum computer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sinasaklaw ng tutorial na ito ang user experience mula sa dalawang pananaw: ang\n"
"physical problem na natutukoy ng mga initial conditions, at ang algorithmic\n"
"component sa paglutas ng isang fluid dynamics example sa isang quantum computer.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Computational Fluid Dynamics (CFD) has a broad range of applications, and thus it is\n"
"important to study and solve the underlying PDEs. An important family of PDEs\n"
"are the Navier-Stokes equations, which are a system of nonlinear partial\n"
"differential equations describing the motion of fluids. They are highly relevant\n"
"for scientific problems and engineering applications.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang Computational Fluid Dynamics (CFD) ay may malawak na hanay ng mga aplikasyon, at samakatuwid ay\n"
"mahalaga na pag-aralan at lutasin ang pinagbabatayan na mga PDEs. Ang isang mahalagang pamilya ng mga PDEs\n"
"ay ang mga Navier-Stokes equations, na isang sistema ng nonlinear partial\n"
"differential equations na naglalarawan ng paggalaw ng mga likido. Lubhang may kaugnayan ang mga ito\n"
"para sa mga scientific problems at engineering applications.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Under certain conditions, the Navier-Stokes equations reduce to Burgers'\n"
"equation, a convection–diffusion equation describing phenomena occurring in\n"
"fluid dynamics, gas dynamics, and nonlinear acoustics, to name a few, by modeling\n"
"dissipative systems.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa ilalim ng ilang kundisyon, ang mga Navier-Stokes equations ay nabawasan sa Burgers'\n"
"equation, isang convection–diffusion equation na naglalarawan ng mga phenomena na nangyayari sa\n"
"fluid dynamics, gas dynamics, at nonlinear acoustics, upang pangalanan ang ilan, sa pamamagitan ng pagmodelo ng\n"
"dissipative systems.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The one-dimensional version of the equation depends on two variables:\n"
"$t \\in \\mathbb{R}_{\\geq 0}$ modeling the temporal dimension, $x \\in \\mathbb{R}$\n"
"representing the spatial dimension. The general form of the equation is called\n"
"the viscous Burgers' equation and reads:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang one-dimensional version ng equation ay umaasa sa dalawang variables:\n"
"$t \\in \\mathbb{R}_{\\geq 0}$ na nagmo-modelo ng temporal dimension, $x \\in \\mathbb{R}$\n"
"na kumakatawan sa spatial dimension. Ang pangkalahatang anyo ng equation ay tinatawag na\n"
"viscous Burgers' equation at nagsasaad:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial t} + u \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} = "
"\\nu \\frac{\\partial^2 u}{\\partial^2 x},$\n"
msgstr ""
"$\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial t} + u \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} = "
"\\nu \\frac{\\partial^2 u}{\\partial^2 x},$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $u(x,t)$ is the fluid speed field at a given position $x$ and time $t$, and $\\nu$\n"
"is the viscosity of the fluid. Viscosity is an important property of a fluid\n"
"that measures its rate-dependent resistance to motion or deformation, and thus it\n"
"plays a crucial role in the determination of the dynamics of a fluid. When the\n"
"viscosity of the fluid is null ($\\nu$ = 0), the equation becomes a conservation\n"
"equation that can develop discontinuities (shock waves), due to the lack of its\n"
"internal resistance. In this case, the equation is called the inviscid Burgers'\n"
"equation and is a special case of nonlinear wave equation.\n"
msgstr ""
"kung saan ang $u(x,t)$ ay ang fluid speed field sa isang ibinigay na posisyon $x$ at oras $t$, at ang $\\nu$\n"
"ay ang viscosity ng likido. Ang viscosity ay isang mahalagang property ng isang likido\n"
"na sumusukat sa rate-dependent resistance nito sa paggalaw o deformation, at samakatuwid ay\n"
"gumaganap ng mahalagang papel sa pagtukoy ng dynamics ng isang likido. Kapag ang\n"
"viscosity ng likido ay null ($\\nu$ = 0), ang equation ay nagiging conservation\n"
"equation na maaaring makabuo ng mga discontinuities (shock waves), dahil sa kakulangan ng\n"
"internal resistance nito. Sa kasong ito, ang equation ay tinatawag na inviscid Burgers'\n"
"equation at isang special case ng nonlinear wave equation.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Strictly speaking, inviscid flows do not occur in nature, but when modeling\n"
"aerodynamic flow, due to the infinitesimal effect of transport, using an\n"
"inviscid description of the problem can be useful. Surprisingly, more than\n"
"70% of aerodynamic theory deals with inviscid flows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mahigpit na sinasalita, ang mga inviscid flows ay hindi nangyayari sa kalikasan, ngunit kapag nagmo-modelo ng\n"
"aerodynamic flow, dahil sa infinitesimal effect ng transport, ang paggamit ng isang\n"
"inviscid description ng problema ay maaaring maging kapaki-pakinabang. Nakakagulat na higit sa\n"
"70% ng aerodynamic theory ay tumatalakay sa mga inviscid flows.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This tutorial uses the inviscid Burgers' equation as a CFD example to solve\n"
"on IBM&reg; QPUs using QUICK-PDE, given by the equation:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ginagamit ng tutorial na ito ang inviscid Burgers' equation bilang isang CFD example upang lutasin\n"
"sa mga IBM&reg; QPUs gamit ang QUICK-PDE, na ibinibigay ng equation:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial t} + u\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} = 0 $\n"
msgstr "$\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial t} + u\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} = 0 $\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The initial condition for this problem is set to a linear function:\n"
"$u(t=0,x) = ax + b,\\text{ with }a,b\\in\\mathbb{R}$\n"
"where $a$ and $b$ are arbitrary constants influencing the shape of the\n"
"solution. You can adjust $a$ and $b$ and see how they influence the\n"
"solving process and the solution.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang initial condition para sa problemang ito ay nakatakda sa isang linear function:\n"
"$u(t=0,x) = ax + b,\\text{ with }a,b\\in\\mathbb{R}$\n"
"kung saan ang $a$ at $b$ ay arbitrary constants na nakakaimpluwensya sa hugis ng\n"
"solusyon. Maaari mong isaayos ang $a$ at $b$ at tingnan kung paano nila naimpluwensyahan ang\n"
"proseso ng paglutas at ang solusyon.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 2 (if needed): Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution "
"{#step-2-if-needed-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr ""
"Hakbang 2 (kung kinakailangan): I-optimize ang problema para sa quantum "
"hardware execution {#step-2-if-needed-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-"
"execution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By default, the solver uses physically-informed parameters, which are "
"initial circuit parameters for a given qubit number and depth from which our"
" solver will start.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa default, ginagamit ng solver ang physically-informed parameters, na mga "
"initial circuit parameters para sa isang ibinigay na qubit number at depth "
"mula sa kung saan magsisimula ang aming solver.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The shots are also part of the parameters with a default value, since fine-"
"tuning them is important.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga shots ay bahagi rin ng mga parameters na may default value, dahil "
"mahalaga ang fine-tuning ng mga ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Depending on the configuration you're trying to solve, the algorithm's\n"
"parameters to achieve satisfactory solutions might need to be adapted; for example, it\n"
"can require more or fewer qubits per variable $t$ and $x$, depending on $a$ and\n"
"$b$. The following adjusts the number of qubits per function per\n"
"variable, the depth per function, and the number of shots.\n"
msgstr ""
"Depende sa configuration na sinusubukan mong lutasin, maaaring kailangang isaayos ang\n"
"parameters ng algorithm upang makamit ang kasiya-siyang mga solusyon; halimbawa,\n"
"maaaring mangailangan ito ng mas marami o mas kaunting qubits bawat variable $t$ at $x$, depende sa $a$ at\n"
"$b$. Iniaayos ng sumusunod ang bilang ng mga qubits bawat function bawat\n"
"variable, ang depth bawat function, at ang bilang ng mga shots.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "You can also see how to specify the backend and the execution mode.\n"
msgstr "Makikita rin kung paano tukuyin ang backend at ang execution mode.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In addition, physically-informed parameters might steer the optimization process\n"
"in a wrong direction; in that case, you can disable it by setting the\n"
"`initialization` strategy to `\"RANDOM\"`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bilang karagdagan, ang physically-informed parameters ay maaaring mag-steer ng optimization process\n"
"sa maling direksyon; sa kasong iyan, maaari mong i-disable ito sa pamamagitan ng pagtakda ng\n"
"`initialization` strategy sa `\"RANDOM\"`.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 3: Compare the algorithm performances {#step-3-compare-the-algorithm-"
"performances}"
msgstr ""
"Hakbang 3: Ikumpara ang mga pagganap ng algorithm {#step-3-compare-the-"
"algorithm-performances}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can compare the convergence process of our solution (HDES) of job_2 to "
"the performance of a physics-informed neural networks (PINN) algorithm and "
"solver (see the [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1711.10561) and the associated"
" [GitHub repository](https://github.com/314arhaam/burger-pinn)).\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari mong ikumpara ang convergence process ng aming solusyon (HDES) ng "
"job_2 sa performance ng isang physics-informed neural networks (PINN) "
"algorithm at solver (tingnan ang [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1711.10561) "
"at ang kaugnay na [GitHub repository](https://github.com/314arhaam/burger-"
"pinn)).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the example of job_2's output (quantum-based approach), only  13 parameters (12 circuit parameters plus 1 scaling parameter) are optimized with the classical solver.\n"
"The convergence process is as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa halimbawa ng output ng job_2 (quantum-based approach), tanging 13 parameters (12 circuit parameters plus 1 scaling parameter) ay na-optimize gamit ang classical solver.\n"
"Ang convergence process ay sumusunod:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"That means a loss below 0.0015 can be reached after 28 iterations, and with "
"optimizing only a few classical parameters.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nangangahulugan ito na ang isang loss na mas mababa sa 0.0015 ay maaabot "
"pagkatapos ng 28 iterations, at sa pag-optimize lamang ng ilang classical "
"parameters.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we can compare the same to the PINN solution with the default configuration suggested by the paper using a gradient-based optimizer. The equivalent of our circuit with 13 parameters to be optimized is the neural network, which requires at least eight layers of 20 neurons, and thus involves optimizing 3021 parameters.\n"
"Then, the target loss is reached at Step 315, loss: 0.0014988397.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayon ay maaari nating ikumpara ang pareho sa PINN solution gamit ang default configuration na iminungkahi ng paper gamit ang isang gradient-based optimizer. Ang katumbas ng aming circuit na may 13 parameters na i-optimize ay ang neural network, na nangangailangan ng hindi bababa sa walong layers ng 20 neurons, at samakatuwid ay nagsasangkot ng pag-optimize ng 3021 parameters.\n"
"Pagkatapos, ang target loss ay naabot sa Step 315, loss: 0.0014988397.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Graph showing PINN data compared with the HDES-Qiskit "
"function.](/docs/images/tutorials/colibritd-pde/pinn-data.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Graph na nagpapakita ng PINN data kumpara sa HDES-Qiskit "
"function.](/docs/images/tutorials/colibritd-pde/pinn-data.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now, since we want to do a fair comparison, we should use the same optimizer in both cases.\n"
"The lowest number of iterations we found for 12 layers of 20 neurons = 4701 parameters:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayon, dahil nais nating gumawa ng patas na pagkukumpara, dapat nating gamitin ang parehong optimizer sa parehong kaso.\n"
"Ang pinakamababang bilang ng iterations na nahanap namin para sa 12 layers ng 20 neurons = 4701 parameters:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can do the same with your data from job_2, and plot a comparison to the "
"PINN solution.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari mong gawin ang pareho gamit ang iyong data mula sa job_2, at mag-plot"
" ng pagkukumpara sa PINN solution.\n"

